310
00:23:55,101 --> 00:23:57,235
We shared a room, didn't we?

311
00:24:00,239 --> 00:24:01,439
That's...

312
00:24:06,011 --> 00:24:09,447
Fine. You two can keep sharing it for all I care.

313
00:24:13,085 --> 00:24:14,385
Mi Young!

314
00:24:15,321 --> 00:24:17,055
It's not like that!

315
00:24:20,293 --> 00:24:21,459
Oh, great.

316
00:24:28,968 --> 00:24:31,002
Just perfect.

317
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:33,782
Verbal abuse, swearing, physical violence, neglect,

318
00:24:33,806 --> 00:24:35,451
and now adultery on top of all that.

319
00:24:35,475 --> 00:24:39,010
You've officially hit the jackpot.

320
00:24:39,812 --> 00:24:42,424
Knock it off. I'm not in the mood for jokes.

321
00:24:42,448 --> 00:24:43,448
A joke?

322
00:24:43,815 --> 00:24:44,993
I'm just laying out the facts.

323
00:24:45,017 --> 00:24:47,595
How did things end up like this?

324
00:24:47,619 --> 00:24:49,687
All I did was sleep and wake up.

325
00:24:50,389 --> 00:24:52,167
What am I supposed to do now?

326
00:24:52,191 --> 00:24:53,172
What do you think?

327
00:24:53,196 --> 00:24:55,827
Brace yourself for the fallout.

328
00:24:56,462 --> 00:24:57,529
The fallout?

329
00:24:58,564 --> 00:25:02,410
This is why men need to watch out for booze and women.

330
00:25:02,434 --> 00:25:05,637
Right when you needed to be on your absolute best behavior,

331
00:25:06,372 --> 00:25:07,873
you went and slept with someone.

332
00:25:08,507 --> 00:25:11,219
"Slept with" is a bit much.

333
00:25:11,243 --> 00:25:12,577
Technically,

334
00:25:13,479 --> 00:25:15,546
they were twin beds.

335
00:25:18,050 --> 00:25:19,961
Your timing couldn't be worse.

336
00:25:19,985 --> 00:25:21,577
You caused a massive train wreck

337
00:25:21,601 --> 00:25:23,722
right before we were about to submit our response.

338
00:25:32,131 --> 00:25:40,131
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

339
00:25:46,445 --> 00:25:47,856
I'm sorry.

340
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:50,248
I must have the wrong room.

341
00:25:51,450 --> 00:25:54,251
Hee Ju, wait, talk to me for a second.

342
00:25:56,221 --> 00:25:58,923
We were just having drinks, and we were so exhausted

343
00:25:59,625 --> 00:26:01,526
that we ended up sleeping together.

344
00:26:27,853 --> 00:26:29,187
Mi Young, let's grab some cof...

345
00:26:38,197 --> 00:26:42,800
The tension was insane, like the calm before a storm.

346
00:26:43,402 --> 00:26:45,403
Mi Young's face looked just like...

347
00:26:45,771 --> 00:26:49,491
Admiral Yi Sun Sin's right before heading into battle.

348
00:26:49,641 --> 00:26:52,910
How on earth do you know what Admiral Yi Sun Sin looked like?

349
00:26:52,935 --> 00:26:56,938
It's a figure of speech!

350
00:26:59,284 --> 00:27:00,818
Still, why?

351
00:27:01,653 --> 00:27:05,556
The event went so well yesterday, and the mood was great.

352
00:27:07,626 --> 00:27:11,262
Did she and Mr. Ji fight again on the way home?

353
00:27:11,997 --> 00:27:14,277
Whatever's going on between them is none of our business.

354
00:27:14,533 --> 00:27:16,511
Stay out of it, Ms. Song.

355
00:27:16,535 --> 00:27:18,880
When did I ever butt in?

356
00:27:18,904 --> 00:27:21,249
You're always meddling.

357
00:27:21,273 --> 00:27:22,874
Always chirping in Ms. Baek's ear

358
00:27:22,975 --> 00:27:25,310
like a little sparrow.

359
00:27:26,779 --> 00:27:27,979
A sparrow?

360
00:27:30,083 --> 00:27:33,228
Want me to peck your eyes out?

361
00:27:33,252 --> 00:27:35,097
I'll show you what this sparrow can do.

362
00:27:35,121 --> 00:27:37,365
- What's with you?
- Chirp-chirp.

363
00:27:37,390 --> 00:27:38,923
Cut it out.

364
00:27:38,948 --> 00:27:40,580
Chirp-chirp.

365
00:27:51,236 --> 00:27:53,436
Why did she have to show up right at that exact second?

366
00:27:54,940 --> 00:27:56,841
She even brought me a change of clothes.

367
00:27:57,376 --> 00:27:59,944
She doesn't usually care what I wear or eat.

368
00:28:00,379 --> 00:28:02,157
Of all days, why today?

369
00:28:02,181 --> 00:28:04,326
And of all days,

370
00:28:04,350 --> 00:28:06,528
why did you have to go and cheat yesterday?

371
00:28:06,552 --> 00:28:08,731
Right before your wife walked in.

372
00:28:08,755 --> 00:28:10,799
I told you, I didn't cheat!

373
00:28:10,823 --> 00:28:13,267
Fine. Let's use the legal term then.

374
00:28:13,291 --> 00:28:14,291
Infidelity.

375
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:18,195
Seriously...

376
00:28:19,398 --> 00:28:21,276
Does this mean...

377
00:28:21,300 --> 00:28:24,736
I'll have to settle the divorce on her terms?

378
00:28:24,870 --> 00:28:26,814
I'll try to spin it somehow,

379
00:28:26,838 --> 00:28:29,373
but the odds are heavily stacked against us.

380
00:28:29,942 --> 00:28:32,810
Unless they screw up even worse than you did...

381
00:28:33,712 --> 00:28:36,758
Fat chance. You know how meticulous she is.

382
00:28:36,782 --> 00:28:37,782
In that case,

383
00:28:38,617 --> 00:28:40,351
you'd better watch your step.

384
00:28:40,652 --> 00:28:41,885
From here on out,

385
00:28:42,254 --> 00:28:43,821
don't even go near a match.

386
00:28:44,757 --> 00:28:46,957
Be on high alert.

387
00:28:47,726 --> 00:28:48,726
High alert.

388
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:56,867
Kyung Tae.

389
00:28:58,971 --> 00:28:59,971
What?

390
00:29:00,739 --> 00:29:02,139
He came by the office?

391
00:29:05,444 --> 00:29:08,413
Our hotel is celebrating its 40th anniversary this year.

392
00:29:09,182 --> 00:29:10,925
We're planning to host

393
00:29:10,949 --> 00:29:13,684
a vow renewal package for our senior guests.

394
00:29:14,687 --> 00:29:17,221
We'd love to collaborate with J&amp;WHITE on this.

395
00:29:17,758 --> 00:29:19,824
Since it's our 40th anniversary event,

396
00:29:20,259 --> 00:29:23,795
it'll be great publicity for both of us.

397
00:29:24,096 --> 00:29:26,831
From the studio to the dresses and makeup...

398
00:29:27,133 --> 00:29:30,869
We'll cover all the expenses for the entire project.

399
00:29:32,571 --> 00:29:35,841
Why are you so keen on working with us specifically?

400
00:29:36,608 --> 00:29:38,010
Do I really need to spell it out?

401
00:29:43,549 --> 00:29:44,549
Right.

402
00:29:44,951 --> 00:29:47,918
Working with me would make things awkward for your husband too.

403
00:29:50,489 --> 00:29:52,857
Anyway, think it over and let me know.

404
00:29:57,229 --> 00:30:00,298
Nothing happened between us yesterday, right?

405
00:30:00,885 --> 00:30:02,265
We were just having drinks,

406
00:30:02,289 --> 00:30:03,697
and we were so exhausted

407
00:30:03,750 --> 00:30:05,877
that we ended up sleeping together.

408
00:30:09,608 --> 00:30:10,608
All right.

409
00:30:11,843 --> 00:30:13,203
There's no reason to turn it down.

410
00:30:15,047 --> 00:30:18,050
Looking at it now, it's a great opportunity for us too.

411
00:30:18,850 --> 00:30:20,352
Let's do the collaboration.

412
00:30:50,581 --> 00:30:51,615
Hello, Mr. Ji.

413
00:30:53,219 --> 00:30:56,454
It's an honor to work with you again.

414
00:30:56,755 --> 00:30:57,922
What did you say?

415
00:30:58,657 --> 00:31:00,658
He's just a business partner.

416
00:31:02,896 --> 00:31:04,662
And like the vice president said,

417
00:31:05,230 --> 00:31:07,432
this collaboration is a huge opportunity for us.

418
00:31:07,767 --> 00:31:10,611
So there's no reason to turn it down.

419
00:31:10,635 --> 00:31:12,346
What do you mean there's no reason?

420
00:31:12,371 --> 00:31:14,805
I haven't even agreed to this yet.

421
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:17,840
You should've discussed it with me before making a decision like this.

422
00:31:17,909 --> 00:31:21,345
And did you discuss it with me before sleeping with that woman?

423
00:31:21,546 --> 00:31:22,546
What?

424
00:31:23,846 --> 00:31:25,293
I made it very clear earlier.

425
00:31:25,317 --> 00:31:27,418
Nothing happened. I swear.

426
00:31:28,687 --> 00:31:30,488
And Hee Ju and I...

427
00:31:30,890 --> 00:31:32,924
It's not what you think between us.

428
00:31:33,058 --> 00:31:35,493
Then what kind of relationship is it?

429
00:31:37,296 --> 00:31:38,296
I mean...

430
00:31:39,265 --> 00:31:41,425
We were just leaning on each other during tough times.

431
00:31:41,466 --> 00:31:42,743
Right.

432
00:31:42,767 --> 00:31:45,880
Exactly how much comforting did you need to end up in a motel?

433
00:31:45,904 --> 00:31:48,172
Do you really have to put it like that?

434
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:50,563
Anyway, we need to discuss working with Calvin

435
00:31:50,587 --> 00:31:52,076
before you make any final calls.

436
00:31:52,577 --> 00:31:54,745
No, I'm not reconsidering.

437
00:31:55,013 --> 00:31:56,093
I'm moving forward with it.

438
00:31:56,248 --> 00:31:57,248
What?

439
00:31:57,784 --> 00:32:00,885
As CEO, I simply made a rational business decision.

440
00:32:01,020 --> 00:32:02,920
The employees were completely on board too.

441
00:32:03,188 --> 00:32:06,357
So don't ruin this. Just go along with it.

442
00:32:06,825 --> 00:32:08,803
"Go along with it?"

443
00:32:08,827 --> 00:32:10,194
What am I, your dog?

444
00:32:11,263 --> 00:32:12,263
Oh, right.

445
00:32:12,431 --> 00:32:14,498
The deadline to submit our response is coming up.

446
00:32:14,632 --> 00:32:15,632
Don't miss it.

447
00:32:19,805 --> 00:32:20,972
Unbelievable.

448
00:32:22,874 --> 00:32:24,474
She's getting back at you, isn't she?

449
00:32:25,544 --> 00:32:26,310
Payback?

450
00:32:26,478 --> 00:32:28,679
"How dare you stay at a motel with another woman?"

451
00:32:29,114 --> 00:32:32,050
"Fine, then I'll work with my ex and not give a damn what you think."

452
00:32:32,617 --> 00:32:35,553
"Starting today, I'm his work wife."

453
00:32:36,888 --> 00:32:37,698
Just like that.

454
00:32:37,722 --> 00:32:39,289
A work wife?

455
00:32:39,558 --> 00:32:41,026
I'm kidding.

456
00:32:41,793 --> 00:32:44,828
I really shouldn't have had so much to drink yesterday.

457
00:32:45,163 --> 00:32:47,998
But seriously, nothing happened between you two?

458
00:32:50,168 --> 00:32:52,236
You said you totally blacked out.

459
00:32:52,671 --> 00:32:54,782
What if something actually did happen?

460
00:32:54,806 --> 00:32:56,907
Absolutely nothing happened.

461
00:32:57,443 --> 00:32:59,987
No matter how drunk I get, I would never cross that line.

462
00:33:00,011 --> 00:33:02,790
You know I've always kept things strictly clean when it comes to women.

463
00:33:02,814 --> 00:33:04,014
I know.

464
00:33:04,383 --> 00:33:07,018
I know better than anyone that you don't mess around with women.

465
00:33:08,587 --> 00:33:12,400
If she uses work as an excuse to fool around with Calvin,

466
00:33:12,424 --> 00:33:13,624
I'm not going to let it slide.

467
00:33:14,192 --> 00:33:15,225
And then what?

468
00:33:15,961 --> 00:33:16,613
What?

469
00:33:16,637 --> 00:33:18,572
You're going to pick a fight with Calvin?

470
00:33:18,597 --> 00:33:20,798
If I have to, I'll do a lot more than that.

471
00:33:45,590 --> 00:33:48,959
It's not what you think between us.

472
00:33:49,127 --> 00:33:51,595
Then what kind of relationship is it?

473
00:33:51,930 --> 00:33:52,930
I mean...

474
00:33:53,666 --> 00:33:55,826
We were just leaning on each other during tough times.

475
00:34:30,636 --> 00:34:33,404
Mi Young walked out first like this.

476
00:34:34,506 --> 00:34:36,508
And Won Ho went running right after her.

477
00:34:38,743 --> 00:34:41,178
Then what on earth is going on with her?

478
00:34:43,982 --> 00:34:46,317
What are you doing right now?

479
00:34:48,754 --> 00:34:50,421
Setting out drinks?

480
00:34:50,989 --> 00:34:53,457
Mom, Mi Young came by yesterday.

481
00:34:53,992 --> 00:34:55,169
What was that sly fox doing here?

482
00:34:55,193 --> 00:34:56,928
She brought Won Ho clothes and underwear.

483
00:34:57,862 --> 00:35:00,182
Is she still looking out for him because he's her husband?

484
00:35:00,465 --> 00:35:01,465
But there was

485
00:35:01,900 --> 00:35:03,500
another woman there besides Mi Young.

486
00:35:05,103 --> 00:35:06,103
Another woman?

487
00:35:06,305 --> 00:35:08,604
- Who?
- I don't know either.

488
00:35:09,242 --> 00:35:12,176
But she left with Won Ho.

489
00:35:13,245 --> 00:35:14,613
With Mi Young, that makes three.

490
00:35:14,845 --> 00:35:16,980
Make some sense.

491
00:35:17,249 --> 00:35:20,098
Are you saying all three of them were at the motel yesterday?

492
00:35:20,122 --> 00:35:21,719
That's what I'm telling you!

493
00:35:22,288 --> 00:35:24,221
I can't wrap my head around it either.

494
00:35:26,291 --> 00:35:28,225
He's seeing another woman?

495
00:35:53,691 --> 00:35:55,359
Bae Su Ji?

496
00:36:13,238 --> 00:36:15,173
You're young, but you really know your stuff.

497
00:36:15,507 --> 00:36:16,507
Impressive work.

498
00:36:17,042 --> 00:36:18,042
Thank you.

499
00:36:18,443 --> 00:36:21,245
Isn't Mr. Ji here today?

500
00:36:22,915 --> 00:36:24,382
He was swamped today,

501
00:36:24,816 --> 00:36:26,216
so I came on his behalf.

502
00:36:27,386 --> 00:36:28,386
I see.

503
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:55,612
(An Hee Ju)

504
00:36:57,983 --> 00:36:58,983
(An Hee Ju)

505
00:37:03,552 --> 00:37:06,133
From here on out, don't even go near a match.

506
00:37:06,158 --> 00:37:08,426
Always watch out for fire.

507
00:37:09,061 --> 00:37:11,762
Right. Stay away from fire.

508
00:37:19,504 --> 00:37:21,940
My hair just isn't coming together today.

509
00:37:25,344 --> 00:37:27,024
Don't tell me you're still hung up on her.

510
00:37:27,312 --> 00:37:28,088
What?

511
00:37:28,112 --> 00:37:31,692
Why are you trying so hard just to see your ex-wife?

512
00:37:31,716 --> 00:37:33,840
Ha Neul said he wanted to see his mom at work,

513
00:37:33,864 --> 00:37:34,864
so I'm taking him.

514
00:37:35,787 --> 00:37:37,021
But you never know.

515
00:37:37,289 --> 00:37:40,225
There might be people from the film industry there.

516
00:37:40,458 --> 00:37:42,025
And if an opportunity comes up,

517
00:37:42,761 --> 00:37:43,928
I can pitch my screenplay.

518
00:37:44,286 --> 00:37:47,132
First impressions are everything, you know.

519
00:37:47,499 --> 00:37:49,666
You're going to Ha Neul's mom's production company?

520
00:37:50,568 --> 00:37:51,568
Yes.

521
00:37:53,238 --> 00:37:54,481
And where are you off to?

522
00:37:54,506 --> 00:37:56,173
I'm going tiger hunting.

523
00:38:03,591 --> 00:38:04,557
(Vow Renewal Wedding)

524
00:38:04,582 --> 00:38:07,351
We've finalized the participants for the event,

525
00:38:08,019 --> 00:38:09,586
so I think we're ready to get started.

526
00:38:10,889 --> 00:38:13,449
I look forward to working with you. Please take good care of us.

527
00:38:13,525 --> 00:38:15,960
What's to take care of? We're all getting paid for this.

528
00:38:18,330 --> 00:38:20,832
And next time,

529
00:38:21,198 --> 00:38:23,133
you can just send an employee.

530
00:38:23,802 --> 00:38:25,636
You're the CEO of a hotel.

531
00:38:25,938 --> 00:38:28,972
Isn't it overkill to deliver documents like this in person?

532
00:38:30,075 --> 00:38:31,542
All right, will do.

533
00:38:32,844 --> 00:38:33,910
But today,

534
00:38:34,479 --> 00:38:36,413
I have something I wanted to give you in person.

535
00:38:45,057 --> 00:38:46,057
This is...

536
00:38:47,358 --> 00:38:48,358
Yes.

537
00:38:49,227 --> 00:38:50,794
It's the ring

538
00:38:51,096 --> 00:38:52,662
your late mother gave me.

539
00:38:54,733 --> 00:38:58,036
She gave me this precious ring and asked me to take good care of you,

540
00:38:59,050 --> 00:39:00,662
but I missed the chance to return it,

541
00:39:00,707 --> 00:39:02,507
and ended up holding onto it all this time.

542
00:39:04,776 --> 00:39:05,909
I thought

543
00:39:06,644 --> 00:39:08,912
today was the right day to give it back.

544
00:39:10,215 --> 00:39:11,215
Today is

545
00:39:12,449 --> 00:39:14,089
the anniversary of your parents' passing.

546
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:23,894
You remembered?

547
00:39:25,130 --> 00:39:26,898
I've never forgotten it for a single moment.

548
00:39:31,336 --> 00:39:33,538
Oh, you have company.

549
00:39:34,005 --> 00:39:35,572
Should I come back later?

550
00:39:35,739 --> 00:39:36,739
No, it's fine.

551
00:39:37,776 --> 00:39:38,776
I'll head out then.

552
00:39:43,448 --> 00:39:44,448
Well, well.

553
00:39:44,582 --> 00:39:46,084
I didn't expect to run into you here.

554
00:39:46,786 --> 00:39:47,951
Right.

555
00:39:48,953 --> 00:39:49,953
Hello.

556
00:39:49,988 --> 00:39:51,655
Hello.

557
00:39:58,429 --> 00:39:59,429
Hey.

558
00:40:00,398 --> 00:40:01,666
That guy just now...

559
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:03,701
Excuse me for a moment, Ms. Jeon.

560
00:40:11,709 --> 00:40:12,742
Hold on.

561
00:40:15,780 --> 00:40:16,780
Take this with you.

562
00:40:19,737 --> 00:40:22,739
My mom gave that to you, so you should have it.

563
00:40:24,122 --> 00:40:25,122
And...

564
00:40:25,990 --> 00:40:28,258
Thank you for remembering her death anniversary.

565
00:40:37,068 --> 00:40:38,068
There's

566
00:40:38,570 --> 00:40:39,747
nothing going on between them, right?

567
00:40:39,771 --> 00:40:41,539
I'm just misunderstanding it, right?

568
00:40:42,007 --> 00:40:44,407
Well, aren't you spinning a whole romance story out of this?

569
00:40:46,879 --> 00:40:48,545
Why are you asking me?

570
00:40:49,013 --> 00:40:50,080
If you're that curious,

571
00:40:50,414 --> 00:40:52,682
there's a fortune teller up the road. Go ask them.

572
00:40:54,999 --> 00:40:57,701
And you say you want a divorce.

573
00:40:58,106 --> 00:41:00,774
My wife used to really hate that bastard.

574
00:41:00,858 --> 00:41:03,160
But something was different today.

575
00:41:03,895 --> 00:41:05,462
The atmosphere between them

576
00:41:05,631 --> 00:41:07,464
was clearly different from usual.

577
00:41:08,600 --> 00:41:09,833
If it bothers you that much,

578
00:41:10,768 --> 00:41:13,237
write a love letter instead of a written response.

579
00:41:13,538 --> 00:41:14,838
That'll be more honest.

580
00:41:20,145 --> 00:41:21,912
- Excuse me.
- Sure.

581
00:41:22,199 --> 00:41:23,199
(Madam Ryu)

582
00:41:24,249 --> 00:41:25,249
Yes, what?

583
00:41:26,417 --> 00:41:28,752
I'm meeting with my lawyer right now. What is it?

584
00:41:30,722 --> 00:41:33,156
What do you mean, I have a woman?

585
00:41:33,391 --> 00:41:35,926
That's not it! What nonsense is Seung Ho talking about?

586
00:41:36,895 --> 00:41:38,546
I don't know! I'm busy. Bye.

587
00:41:38,630 --> 00:41:39,763
Damn it, seriously.

588
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:42,198
Gosh.

589
00:41:42,833 --> 00:41:44,477
Who was that, for you to talk like that?

590
00:41:44,568 --> 00:41:46,069
Just a loan shark.

591
00:41:46,604 --> 00:41:49,106
Where were we just now?

592
00:41:50,808 --> 00:41:54,677
Are you the lawyer, Bae Su Ji?

593
00:41:55,446 --> 00:41:56,846
Yes, I am.

594
00:41:57,115 --> 00:41:59,400
You're Bae Su Ji? You wench!

595
00:41:59,484 --> 00:42:02,663
You bitch! Who taught you

596
00:42:02,687 --> 00:42:03,887
to be a gold digger like that!

597
00:42:04,105 --> 00:42:05,105
It's my mom.

598
00:42:05,156 --> 00:42:07,310
How dare you!

599
00:42:07,394 --> 00:42:09,142
- Let go!
- How can you be like this!

600
00:42:09,226 --> 00:42:10,577
Are you not ashamed of yourself?

601
00:42:10,661 --> 00:42:12,512
What are you doing, Mom?

602
00:42:12,596 --> 00:42:13,596
You crazy bastard!

603
00:42:13,833 --> 00:42:16,517
You bastard! Can't you tell a lawyer from a gold digger?

604
00:42:16,612 --> 00:42:17,994
- You little bastard!
- Mom!

605
00:42:18,370 --> 00:42:19,520
Ma'am! Please, calm down!

606
00:42:19,604 --> 00:42:20,513
Move!

607
00:42:20,537 --> 00:42:21,722
You bastard!

608
00:42:21,806 --> 00:42:23,324
You did all that just to go around

609
00:42:23,408 --> 00:42:24,451
with a young thing like her?

610
00:42:24,475 --> 00:42:26,443
You crazy bastard!

611
00:42:26,911 --> 00:42:28,211
You idiot!

612
00:42:29,014 --> 00:42:31,114
Freeze!

613
00:42:31,723 --> 00:42:33,224
Damn, that hurts!

614
00:42:36,721 --> 00:42:38,655
Ryu Mi Sun.

615
00:42:39,958 --> 00:42:41,792
How have you not changed at all?

616
00:42:43,895 --> 00:42:45,062
Su Ji?

617
00:42:52,296 --> 00:42:53,670
Let's go.

618
00:42:56,007 --> 00:42:57,291
What brings you here?

619
00:42:57,375 --> 00:43:00,043
I'm here to see Ms. Song Woo Young.

620
00:43:00,345 --> 00:43:01,963
We agreed to meet at two.

621
00:43:02,047 --> 00:43:04,265
I see. And you are?

622
00:43:04,349 --> 00:43:07,017
I'm the father of her son.

623
00:43:07,385 --> 00:43:08,796
And he's her son.

624
00:43:08,820 --> 00:43:10,731
Come on, Ha Neul, say hi.

625
00:43:10,755 --> 00:43:12,022
Hello.

626
00:43:12,223 --> 00:43:13,890
Please wait a moment.

627
00:43:33,456 --> 00:43:34,456
Ha Neul.

628
00:43:34,579 --> 00:43:36,046
It seems like your mom's very busy.

629
00:43:36,447 --> 00:43:37,607
Let's come back another time.

630
00:43:41,919 --> 00:43:44,087
(Law Office of Bae Su Ji)

631
00:43:54,132 --> 00:43:56,533
How did you even know I was here, Mom?

632
00:43:56,641 --> 00:43:58,574
What do you mean how?

633
00:43:59,056 --> 00:44:01,824
I saw the business card in your room. That's how.

634
00:44:03,475 --> 00:44:05,575
I never imagined that Bae Su Ji

635
00:44:05,978 --> 00:44:07,378
would be you, Su Ji.

636
00:44:07,644 --> 00:44:09,378
Whether or not you knew it was me,

637
00:44:10,682 --> 00:44:12,949
that was crossing a line.

638
00:44:14,252 --> 00:44:17,505
So you two knew each other back home?

639
00:44:17,589 --> 00:44:18,822
Yes.

640
00:44:19,356 --> 00:44:20,690
And Mr. Kwon.

641
00:44:21,426 --> 00:44:24,561
The three of us were really close.

642
00:44:27,031 --> 00:44:29,299
Anyway, Su Ji, it's really nice to see you again.

643
00:44:30,101 --> 00:44:33,403
I'd heard about you now and then,

644
00:44:33,571 --> 00:44:35,639
but I never knew you were this close by.

645
00:44:36,007 --> 00:44:38,108
I'll come visit often from now on.

646
00:44:38,209 --> 00:44:40,527
No. You don't have to come anymore.

647
00:44:40,611 --> 00:44:42,696
Seeing you once is more than enough.

648
00:44:42,780 --> 00:44:44,915
Come on. Once is not enough.

649
00:44:45,249 --> 00:44:47,784
Su Ji, are you even eating well?

650
00:44:48,053 --> 00:44:51,522
You're even thinner than when you were young.

651
00:44:52,991 --> 00:44:55,091
I'll bring you some side dishes.

652
00:45:01,232 --> 00:45:03,700
Mom, let's go. My consultation is over.

653
00:45:03,968 --> 00:45:06,870
Do you like soy-braised beef? What about pickled wild garlic leaves?

654
00:45:07,571 --> 00:45:10,140
I have some delicious seasoned vegetables at home.

655
00:45:10,374 --> 00:45:11,908
I'll come again, Su Ji.

656
00:45:25,990 --> 00:45:27,157
Mom, Dad...

657
00:45:29,093 --> 00:45:30,360
How are you?

658
00:45:30,394 --> 00:45:32,412
(Baek Chul Gyu, Kang Kyeong Hee)

659
00:45:32,496 --> 00:45:35,216
I've been so caught up with life, I've come way too late, haven't I?

660
00:45:36,200 --> 00:45:37,200
I'm sorry.

661
00:45:41,005 --> 00:45:42,565
It's not like I'm doing anything great.

662
00:45:47,044 --> 00:45:48,745
You only have one daughter,

663
00:45:50,448 --> 00:45:51,448
but I

664
00:45:52,683 --> 00:45:54,717
neglected you, using my hardships as an excuse.

665
00:45:57,255 --> 00:45:58,288
Mom, Dad,

666
00:45:59,491 --> 00:46:00,858
you remember Calvin, right?

667
00:46:03,761 --> 00:46:04,794
Calvin

668
00:46:06,031 --> 00:46:08,298
told me that today is your death anniversary.

669
00:46:13,304 --> 00:46:15,038
The date even I forgot...

670
00:46:16,675 --> 00:46:18,141
Calvin remembered.

671
00:46:24,448 --> 00:46:26,716
I should have lived a better life.

672
00:46:30,688 --> 00:46:31,688
I'm sorry.

673
00:46:32,857 --> 00:46:34,024
I'm sorry, Mom.

674
00:47:07,492 --> 00:47:08,492
One of our employees

675
00:47:09,127 --> 00:47:10,793
made a very big mistake.

676
00:47:11,295 --> 00:47:12,646
While sorting the dress list,

677
00:47:12,730 --> 00:47:14,765
for the senior wedding couples,

678
00:47:15,305 --> 00:47:18,173
she must have mixed up two people with the same name.

679
00:47:18,502 --> 00:47:21,537
The designs and measurements got swapped,

680
00:47:22,873 --> 00:47:25,675
so we'll probably have to remake them.

681
00:47:27,712 --> 00:47:29,012
So that's what happened.

682
00:47:30,248 --> 00:47:32,983
Then are you postponing the wedding date?

683
00:47:33,450 --> 00:47:34,884
That'd be nice,

684
00:47:35,386 --> 00:47:37,754
but the wedding date has already been announced.

685
00:47:38,656 --> 00:47:39,989
Don't worry about that.

686
00:47:40,324 --> 00:47:41,858
I'll take care of it.

687
00:47:42,326 --> 00:47:44,160
I'm sorry for all the trouble.

688
00:47:44,695 --> 00:47:47,463
It's fine. Mistakes can happen while you work.

689
00:47:49,734 --> 00:47:50,900
Don't worry too much.

690
00:47:51,168 --> 00:47:52,368
That's hardly anything.

691
00:47:53,137 --> 00:47:54,897
I can accommodate you however much you need.

692
00:47:58,642 --> 00:48:00,520
Faking smiles, pretending everything's great when it's not,

693
00:48:00,544 --> 00:48:03,045
and putting on a show just to butter people up.

694
00:48:03,648 --> 00:48:04,848
What else would you call that?

695
00:48:05,616 --> 00:48:07,050
I refuse to stoop that low.

696
00:48:07,351 --> 00:48:10,620
So you're not changing the design, no matter what?

697
00:48:10,704 --> 00:48:12,772
No. Absolutely not.

698
00:48:12,857 --> 00:48:15,358
Unless Ms. Cheon asks for it herself, I'm not touching it.

699
00:48:18,062 --> 00:48:19,396
- Mi Young.
- Yes?

700
00:48:20,031 --> 00:48:23,332
Since you're here, do you want to check the wedding hall construction site?

701
00:48:24,002 --> 00:48:25,268
Wedding hall?

702
00:48:25,669 --> 00:48:28,338
We're actually building our own in-house brand wedding hall.

703
00:48:28,840 --> 00:48:29,973
Calvin Wedding Hall.

704
00:48:30,340 --> 00:48:32,475
The interior work isn't done yet,

705
00:48:32,643 --> 00:48:34,411
and it's still at a very early stage.

706
00:48:35,346 --> 00:48:39,015
If you check it out and tell me what you think, I'd like to factor it in.

707
00:48:40,018 --> 00:48:42,019
My opinion doesn't matter that much.

708
00:48:43,154 --> 00:48:44,287
Because it's your opinion.

709
00:48:45,790 --> 00:48:47,357
Anything you tell me

710
00:48:47,593 --> 00:48:49,592
would be a huge help.

711
00:48:51,095 --> 00:48:52,095
That won't work?

712
00:49:17,922 --> 00:49:18,955
Look over there.

713
00:49:20,391 --> 00:49:23,403
That's the indoor wedding hall, right?

714
00:49:23,427 --> 00:49:24,427
That's right.

715
00:49:26,130 --> 00:49:27,941
How's the seating arrangement laid out?

716
00:49:27,965 --> 00:49:29,699
One second. Ms. Park!

717
00:49:30,401 --> 00:49:31,401
Yes, sir!

718
00:49:32,870 --> 00:49:34,871
Let's hear Ms. Beak's opinion on this.

719
00:49:35,040 --> 00:49:36,040
Sure.

720
00:49:38,810 --> 00:49:42,779
It'd be nice if that connected to the stage.

721
00:49:46,784 --> 00:49:50,153
And if the seating arrangements are here, would the doors be over there?

722
00:50:00,831 --> 00:50:02,098
Thank you for today, Mi Young.

723
00:50:02,800 --> 00:50:03,800
No problem.

724
00:50:04,040 --> 00:50:06,541
Anyway, we'll make the dress as soon as possible,

725
00:50:06,698 --> 00:50:08,698
and make sure it doesn't affect the wedding dates.

726
00:50:09,173 --> 00:50:10,173
Okay.

727
00:50:13,244 --> 00:50:14,244
You should go.

728
00:50:14,718 --> 00:50:16,419
Right. Okay.

729
00:50:16,847 --> 00:50:17,847
See you.

730
00:50:30,628 --> 00:50:32,629
What a scene.

731
00:50:34,498 --> 00:50:36,666
So now you're dating for the whole world to see?

732
00:50:38,135 --> 00:50:39,135
What?

733
00:50:39,211 --> 00:50:41,715
You're still on the clock. Don't you think this is too much?

734
00:50:41,739 --> 00:50:43,183
Seriously, what would other people think?

735
00:50:43,207 --> 00:50:44,474
Other people?

736
00:50:46,076 --> 00:50:48,210
You're not the one to be saying that now.

737
00:50:48,446 --> 00:50:49,446
Why not?

738
00:50:49,580 --> 00:50:50,824
Have you ever once seen me

739
00:50:50,848 --> 00:50:52,382
slacking off during work hours?

740
00:50:53,684 --> 00:50:56,419
So you pulled that because it wasn't work hours then?

741
00:50:56,720 --> 00:50:57,720
Pulled that?

742
00:50:57,855 --> 00:51:00,700
What else would you call spending a night with another woman at a motel?

743
00:51:00,724 --> 00:51:03,309
How many times do I have to tell you that's a misunderstanding?

744
00:51:03,393 --> 00:51:05,306
I saw it with my own two eyes.

745
00:51:05,395 --> 00:51:07,146
What's the misunderstanding?

746
00:51:07,230 --> 00:51:10,166
All right. Keep thinking what you want.

747
00:51:13,337 --> 00:51:15,171
Where are you going during work hours?

748
00:51:15,373 --> 00:51:16,473
I'm going to get food.

749
00:51:16,907 --> 00:51:18,908
Because I was too busy working to even eat!

750
00:51:23,547 --> 00:51:24,547
My gosh.

751
00:51:25,249 --> 00:51:27,450
That's not strong enough.

752
00:51:28,364 --> 00:51:31,733
Maybe if there'd at least been some light show of affection...

753
00:51:32,857 --> 00:51:35,091
Just coming out of a motel together

754
00:51:36,027 --> 00:51:38,161
doesn't carry much legal weight either.

755
00:51:40,197 --> 00:51:41,197
I see.

756
00:51:41,471 --> 00:51:43,139
But since we got a lead now,

757
00:51:43,534 --> 00:51:45,702
it's worth keeping an eye out, right?

758
00:51:51,008 --> 00:51:52,175
How do you know...

759
00:51:52,776 --> 00:51:54,143
Calvin?

760
00:51:54,712 --> 00:51:55,712
Sorry?

761
00:51:56,346 --> 00:51:57,380
A few days ago,

762
00:51:58,321 --> 00:51:59,421
at the office.

763
00:52:00,218 --> 00:52:02,185
That...

764
00:52:03,354 --> 00:52:06,556
I've got some work coming up that involves collaborating with him.

765
00:52:08,459 --> 00:52:09,459
I see.

766
00:52:10,532 --> 00:52:12,395
How about you?

767
00:52:13,297 --> 00:52:15,064
How do you know him?

768
00:52:16,000 --> 00:52:19,435
Calvin was my client.

769
00:52:19,870 --> 00:52:23,139
I was his divorce attorney.

770
00:52:24,108 --> 00:52:25,108
I see.

771
00:52:25,809 --> 00:52:28,611
I guess there's something between you and Calvin?

772
00:52:30,748 --> 00:52:31,748
I guess this is

773
00:52:32,516 --> 00:52:33,816
a lawyer's instinct.

774
00:52:37,454 --> 00:52:38,521
Before I got married,

775
00:52:39,657 --> 00:52:41,558
we used to see each other.

776
00:52:42,727 --> 00:52:43,727
Are you...

777
00:52:44,328 --> 00:52:45,428
Calvin's

778
00:52:46,363 --> 00:52:47,363
first love?

779
00:52:50,968 --> 00:52:52,402
What a coincidence.

780
00:52:55,272 --> 00:52:57,440
It's all in the past anyway.

781
00:52:57,708 --> 00:53:00,209
Don't you think it's a bit shocking

782
00:53:01,532 --> 00:53:03,899
to say that it's all in the past?

783
00:53:04,882 --> 00:53:05,882
Sorry?

784
00:53:06,083 --> 00:53:07,083
Do you know

785
00:53:07,820 --> 00:53:10,620
why Calvin got divorced? Actually, no.

786
00:53:11,355 --> 00:53:12,855
Why he got married?

787
00:53:14,358 --> 00:53:15,358
Do you?

788
00:53:16,060 --> 00:53:18,862
Back then, the woman he was seeing behind my back

789
00:53:19,830 --> 00:53:21,030
got pregnant.

790
00:53:22,066 --> 00:53:23,366
I knew it. You don't know.

791
00:53:24,501 --> 00:53:27,136
Honestly, those who know

792
00:53:27,638 --> 00:53:29,105
all know this.

793
00:53:31,008 --> 00:53:32,141
Seven years ago,

794
00:53:33,370 --> 00:53:35,330
it seemed Calvin was battling his half-brothers,

795
00:53:36,187 --> 00:53:38,121
for management rights to the company.

796
00:53:38,415 --> 00:53:39,415
Give him some.

797
00:53:42,086 --> 00:53:43,853
You've had a hard time, right?

798
00:53:44,088 --> 00:53:46,048
Let's forget about all that and just drink today.

799
00:53:46,090 --> 00:53:49,459
The day he went to his parents' house to make up with his half-brothers...

800
00:53:49,994 --> 00:53:50,994
Cheers.

801
00:53:51,061 --> 00:53:52,161
Cheers!

802
00:53:52,296 --> 00:53:53,796
That incident happened.

803
00:53:54,064 --> 00:53:56,032
How about it? Want to go for another round?

804
00:53:56,100 --> 00:53:58,311
It'll be okay. Don't get drunk, okay?

805
00:53:58,335 --> 00:53:59,546
It's okay.

806
00:53:59,570 --> 00:54:00,804
Let's get one more drink.

807
00:54:14,618 --> 00:54:16,552
I'm okay. I'm fine.

808
00:54:35,873 --> 00:54:37,106
His half-brothers

809
00:54:38,142 --> 00:54:40,877
deliberately set him up,

810
00:54:43,914 --> 00:54:45,414
and Calvin fell for it.

811
00:54:45,749 --> 00:54:47,817
He ended up marrying that woman.

812
00:54:54,999 --> 00:54:58,567
His brothers told him that if he gave up his rights,

813
00:54:59,163 --> 00:55:01,397
they'd cover it up.

814
00:55:02,500 --> 00:55:03,500
But...

815
00:55:04,035 --> 00:55:05,768
Calvin said that he didn't want to do that.

816
00:55:08,105 --> 00:55:09,939
It was total drama

817
00:55:10,574 --> 00:55:12,575
involving the entire family.

818
00:55:14,578 --> 00:55:15,578
And

819
00:55:16,847 --> 00:55:18,767
the person who suffered the most from all that

820
00:55:19,489 --> 00:55:20,856
is right in front of me.

821
00:55:36,166 --> 00:55:37,233
Mr. Ji!

822
00:55:37,835 --> 00:55:39,003
Where are you going?

823
00:55:40,771 --> 00:55:41,871
Wait!

824
00:55:50,781 --> 00:55:51,925
Stop!

825
00:55:51,949 --> 00:55:53,516
Why did you run?

826
00:55:54,318 --> 00:55:55,618
Let's do this.

827
00:55:55,753 --> 00:55:58,855
Remember how we were going to meet three times?

828
00:56:00,091 --> 00:56:01,791
Let's just forget that ever happened.

829
00:56:02,425 --> 00:56:03,425
What?

830
00:56:03,494 --> 00:56:04,727
I'm really sorry,

831
00:56:04,795 --> 00:56:07,096
but I'm not really in a position to do that now.

832
00:56:08,232 --> 00:56:10,033
Then you could have just said that.

833
00:56:10,600 --> 00:56:12,202
Why are you making me look like a fool?

834
00:56:13,356 --> 00:56:14,356
Is it because

835
00:56:14,838 --> 00:56:16,239
of your wife?

836
00:56:19,043 --> 00:56:22,611
But that was a misunderstanding! Nothing happened.

837
00:56:22,813 --> 00:56:25,481
But still, she saw us in the motel.

838
00:56:25,916 --> 00:56:27,436
It's natural for her to misunderstand.

839
00:56:28,051 --> 00:56:29,852
If you think so, Mr. Ji,

840
00:56:30,687 --> 00:56:31,967
then I guess it can't be helped.

841
00:56:37,461 --> 00:56:38,461
Right.

842
00:56:38,596 --> 00:56:40,062
Then before I leave,

843
00:56:40,631 --> 00:56:42,165
can I create one misunderstanding?

844
00:56:42,599 --> 00:56:44,433
Create a misunderstanding?

845
00:56:44,969 --> 00:56:46,201
I saw something too.

846
00:56:51,609 --> 00:56:53,943
What other misunderstanding are you trying to make?

847
00:57:13,464 --> 00:57:14,464
Mi Young.

848
00:57:15,299 --> 00:57:16,299
Yes?

849
00:57:16,567 --> 00:57:18,301
What? Is it not to your taste?

850
00:57:19,503 --> 00:57:20,536
It's nothing.

851
00:57:22,606 --> 00:57:23,606
What's going on?

852
00:57:24,040 --> 00:57:26,542
Inviting me out to eat first.

853
00:57:41,825 --> 00:57:43,292
Why didn't you tell me?

854
00:57:44,094 --> 00:57:45,928
Didn't tell you

855
00:57:46,363 --> 00:57:47,363
what?

856
00:57:49,166 --> 00:57:50,867
The day you went by your parents' house

857
00:57:52,502 --> 00:57:53,669
to meet your half-brothers.

858
00:57:56,206 --> 00:57:57,273
You got this.

859
00:57:58,208 --> 00:58:00,376
Answer well when your brothers ask you a question,

860
00:58:01,178 --> 00:58:03,446
and try to laugh even if they aren't funny.

861
00:58:04,181 --> 00:58:06,616
You look like you're mad if you stay still.

862
00:58:07,150 --> 00:58:08,951
They don't care about that.

863
00:58:09,586 --> 00:58:11,132
They don't even like me that much anyway.

864
00:58:11,156 --> 00:58:12,822
But still, they're family.

865
00:58:13,423 --> 00:58:14,324
Your brothers

866
00:58:14,408 --> 00:58:16,942
might have been waiting for you to make the first move.

867
00:58:17,361 --> 00:58:19,138
If you make the first move and approach them,

868
00:58:19,162 --> 00:58:21,430
they'll welcome you warmly even before you know it.

869
00:58:21,899 --> 00:58:24,500
Okay. You're all grown up now, Mi Young.

870
00:58:24,701 --> 00:58:25,868
Treat me with respect now.

871
00:58:32,676 --> 00:58:34,076
Don't worry, I'll do my best.

872
00:58:36,380 --> 00:58:37,380
I love you.

873
00:58:38,015 --> 00:58:39,015
Me too.

874
00:58:39,483 --> 00:58:40,483
You got this!

875
00:58:40,685 --> 00:58:41,685
I got this!

876
00:58:43,688 --> 00:58:44,688
That something,

877
00:58:45,656 --> 00:58:47,790
so unbelievable happened that day.

878
00:58:49,526 --> 00:58:50,659
Why didn't you tell me?

879
00:58:52,362 --> 00:58:53,362
Is that why

880
00:58:53,630 --> 00:58:55,497
you broke up with me?

881
00:58:57,834 --> 00:59:00,274
Because you were scared of being threatened by your brothers?

882
00:59:00,370 --> 00:59:01,370
Or.

883
00:59:02,572 --> 00:59:04,106
Because you just couldn’t

884
00:59:04,642 --> 00:59:06,642
give up your right to the Calvin Hotel management?

885
00:59:08,312 --> 00:59:09,746
I could give up everything,

886
00:59:12,049 --> 00:59:13,816
but not that child.

887
00:59:16,921 --> 00:59:18,788
The baby that woman had back then.

888
00:59:20,958 --> 00:59:21,958
I couldn't

889
00:59:25,095 --> 00:59:26,629
make him illegitimate like me.

890
00:59:28,332 --> 00:59:29,699
Is that why you got a divorce?

891
00:59:30,801 --> 00:59:31,841
Because it was revealed

892
00:59:34,505 --> 00:59:36,605
that the child wasn't yours?

893
00:59:38,241 --> 00:59:39,241
Mi Young.

894
00:59:42,412 --> 00:59:43,412
Do you know...

895
00:59:44,882 --> 00:59:47,316
Do you know how much I hated you all this time?

896
01:00:41,604 --> 01:00:44,440
(Epilogue)

897
01:00:46,510 --> 01:00:47,510
Calvin!

898
01:01:09,866 --> 01:01:12,634
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

899
01:01:14,337 --> 01:01:15,187
What's this?

900
01:01:15,271 --> 01:01:16,638
I changed my mind.

901
01:01:16,973 --> 01:01:20,042
This is what we call backstabbing.

902
01:01:20,977 --> 01:01:22,662
You crazy bastard!

903
01:01:22,746 --> 01:01:25,247
- The code name for this mission is...
- To that place...

904
01:01:26,450 --> 01:01:28,918
Never in my life have I seen something like this.

905
01:01:29,494 --> 01:01:31,139
Bringing a woman

906
01:01:31,223 --> 01:01:32,338
even as he's coming home?

907
01:01:32,422 --> 01:01:33,923
Has he lost his mind?

908
01:01:35,578 --> 01:01:38,212
If you're that jealous, go bring one yourself too.

909
01:01:39,463 --> 01:01:41,181
You should fix that bad habit of yours,

910
01:01:41,265 --> 01:01:43,833
where you blame others while bringing up old wounds!

911
01:01:44,634 --> 01:01:46,234
For crying out loud, shut your mouth.
